    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 1,
        "line": 2,
        "text": "During the war and the German occupation of France, Picasso had been declared a degenerate artiat. Unlike the other so-called degenerate artists, who had taken refuge in America, he had stayed on in his studio in Paris. That was when I first met him."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 13,
        "line": 648,
        "text": "..¿He married Jacqueline and I too married and hag another child and married a second time. But all that is in the future. For the present, this is my moment with and for Picasso...How grateful I felt to him! He had made me strong strong enough to do anything!"
